{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/90256-sidestepping-umbra","id":90256,"title":"Sidestepping / Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-13T09:00:07-07:00","id":90256,"title":"Sidestepping / Umbra","content":"Can werewolves still do this? I haven't read through the book for years. I know it was removed as a built-in skill, but I'm sure I remember it being a 3 or 4 dot gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:35:32-07:00","id":90280,"title":"","content":"I take it you mean Garou from Werewolf the Apocalypse? This is the Forsaken board. Just in case, yes, the Uratha can essentially sidestep at a locus, and there are a bunch of abilities that let them do it faster or away from loci.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T02:42:02-07:00","id":90758,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I should have explained it better. Thanks for your reply.<br /> <br /> I'm running a B&amp;S Vampire game, and I am going to add werewolf protagonist at some point. I've never played W:tF, and I last read the book years ago. This character is going to be smart enough to know when to run, so I was wanting to know if side-stepping was still a viable option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T07:38:03-07:00","id":90892,"title":"","content":"In Forsaken, the ability to &quot;step sideways&quot; remains something that every Werewolf can do. However, in Forsaken, it can only be done in proximity to a &quot;Loci&quot;. A Loci is a magical power point, the closest analog being a caern or a node in Classic World of Darkness. Certain Gifts can expand upon this basic ability. Luckily, Loci are far more common in NWoD and Most Vampires are so spirit-blind that they wouldn't be able to recognize one if they were standing on top of it.<br /> Uratha are not the straight combat monsters the Garou are, so they are more likely to use tactics against a dangerous foe. And The Uratha rarely travel alone..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T10:11:43-07:00","id":90961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/90256-sidestepping-umbra?p=90892#post90892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And The Uratha rarely travel alone..</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for emphasis. A pack instead of a single werewolf is more likely, though their &quot;scout&quot; Auspice (Irraka) could be running solo for a bit and they are the ones most likely to cut &amp; run if they're in too deep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T11:12:24-07:00","id":90986,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that the bigger the locus, the bigger it's area of influence, and the bigger the terrain under which the werewolf can step sideways. For example, a rank 5 locus could cover an entire mountain, so a similar effect could be achieved if the vampires happen on the specific werewolf's turf. Also, keep in mind that those loci are extremely rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T01:48:25-07:00","id":91483,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your input guys, I really appreciate it. I need to re-read that book...<br /> <br /> The Uratha in question will be working solo, but not by choice. His pack are &quot;indisposed&quot; at the moment. Depending on what the players do, they might meet them. And again, depending on the players, they might end up owing them a favour... Or there will be teeth and claws and screaming and blood and death. I always like giving people the choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}